  "date_basis": "chunk_manifest",
  "concise_summary": "PKD develops a hermeneutical theology where the Book of Acts functions as an encoding-decoding grid revealing hidden patterns in reality, history, and his own fiction. He argues that by superimposing Acts as an interpretive lens over his 1974 visions and the novel 'Tears,' one extracts the information that Christ's church is a secret revolutionary underground opposed to the satanic Empire. This framework recasts 2000 years of Christian history as a dialectic between persecuted believers and worldly power, echoing medieval Messianic theology (Joachim del Fiore) and leading to his conclusion that the Holy Spirit, encountered as the personality 'Thomas,' provided this liberating vision.",
  "key_claims": [
    "Acts is not a historical document but an encoding-decoding lens that transforms how one perceives reality across time; it renders space-time as illusion and reveals morphological constants (revolutionary Christianity vs. the Empire).",
    "The information extracted through the Acts grid is Christ himself—identified with VALIS and understood as possessing information metabolism—not as savior from sin but as Messiah founding a literal, earthly millennial kingdom.",
    "Reality itself is structured as Torah: both book (information) and carrier (world), suggesting that applying the Acts grid is analogous to reading the Torah, revealing God's design encoded in history.",
    "The Holy Spirit is a saprophytic life form (Thomas) acting through the Acts grid to manifest Christ's presence and galvanize a revolutionary underground; it accounts for PKD's 2-3-74 visions and the information he later found in encyclopedic sources.",
    "The percipient (PKD himself) discovers he has been living since Pentecost as a contemporary of Christ, participating in Acts outside spatiotemporal reality; his present actions are part of the Acts of the Apostles.",
    "Intellectual exegesis becomes subordinate to direct experiential encounter with God's love and personality (11-17-80); this supersedes theological understanding."
  ],
  "recurring_concepts": [
    "Acts (as encoding-decoding grid/lens)",
    "The Holy Spirit (saprophytic life form; agent of revelation)",
    "The Plasmate (information extracted when Acts grid is applied; Christ)",
